# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify header rules.
# The Vercel equivalent is vercel.json at the repo root — keep the two in sync.
#
# Note what is NOT here: Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy and Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy.
# An earlier version of this port needed both, because expo-sqlite's web backend
# runs SQLite in a worker over SharedArrayBuffer, which browsers only expose to
# cross-origin-isolated pages. That was abandoned (see src/db/driver.web.ts), and
# dropping it matters commercially as well as technically: COEP require-corp
# blocks cross-origin subresources that do not opt in, including ad pixels. This
# app can now sit on the same origin as the marketing site and its Meta pixel.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Never let a browser hold an old service worker.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Metro content-hashes these filenames, so the bytes behind a URL never change.
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Same reasoning, but versioned by package.json rather than by hash — so it is
# revalidated rather than pinned for a year.
/sqljs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
